    "content" : "This past weekend I finally did something that I&#39;ve been meaning to do for a long time - countersink the screws in my Hotplate project so there is more available room to use for reflowing circuit boards. The original writeup is here: <a href=\"http://tinkeringetc.blogspot.com/2011/06/homemade-pid-controlled-hotplate.html\" class=\"ot-anchor\">http://tinkeringetc.blogspot.com/2011/06/homemade-pid-controlled-hotplate.html</a> and you can see that the screws used to stick out of the top limiting the space that could be used. Now that the screws are below the surface, I can place circuit boards that are larger than the surface of the hotplate on top of it, and the circuit board will lay flat.",
    "objectType" : "note",
    "originalContent" : "This past weekend I finally did something that I've been meaning to do for a long time - countersink the screws in my Hotplate project so there is more available room to use for reflowing circuit boards. The original writeup is here: http://tinkeringetc.blogspot.com/2011/06/homemade-pid-controlled-hotplate.html and you can see that the screws used to stick out of the top limiting the space that could be used. Now that the screws are below the surface, I can place circuit boards that are larger than the surface of the hotplate on top of it, and the circuit board will lay flat.",
